Rach2: make udhcpc6 build against the ported musl.

`networking/udhcp/d6_dhcpc.c` includes `<linux/filter.h>`, which the ported
musl does not have, for a BPF block upstream keeps inside `#if 0`, as
`0001-udhcpc-build-against-musl.patch` says of `dhcpc.c`. The include goes;
the rest of the file needs nothing musl lacks.

--- a/networking/udhcp/d6_dhcpc.c
+++ b/networking/udhcp/d6_dhcpc.c
@@ -61,7 +61,8 @@
 
 #include <netinet/if_ether.h>
 #include <netpacket/packet.h>
-#include <linux/filter.h>
+/* Rach2: the ported musl has no <linux/filter.h>, which only the BPF block
+ * below, inside #if 0 upstream, would need. */
 
 /* "struct client_data_t client_data" is in bb_common_bufsiz1 */
 
